<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-07: Intake run orchestrator — IJobHandler stage machine (Receive … Record), resume without re-running AI, atomic claim, terminal-last, per-door/per-harness kill switches, correlationId</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>blocked — tasks 004, 010, 011, 012</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF IJobHandler with idempotency and resume guarantees (fail-open and duplicate-output risks, NFR-01); depends on 3+ tasks; tags bff-api, worker.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>FULL rigor with 4 dependencies, flagged high-risk in plan (critical path; at-least-once safety); new state-machine pattern copied only by rules from the frozen invoice handler.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>004, 010, 011, 012</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, worker, job, di, config, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the intake run orchestrator: one ADR-004 `IJobHandler` (JobType `IntakeRun`) that drives a `sprk_processingjob` run through stages 1–10 of spec FR-07, applying the invoice pipeline's step-0 rules (payload → lock → re-read → terminal-first → flag → resume from stored state) by COPYING the pattern of `InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs` without editing it. It must resume at the failed stage without re-running AI, never duplicate outputs on redelivery, write the terminal status last, honour per-door and per-harness kill switches, and carry correlationId end to end.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF jobs framework (IJobHandler, JobContract, JobOutcome, ServiceBusJobProcessor), atomic idempotency (ADR-004 A1 §4) and Dataverse optimistic concurrency. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Services/Intake/IntakeRunJobHandler.cs` + `Services/Intake/IntakeRunStore.cs` (run/request reads and conditional writes) + `Configuration/IntakePipelineOptions.cs` (kill switches), registered in `JobProcessingModule.cs`; stages persist their results on the run before advancing; Classify uses `IAgreementAi.ClassifyAsync` (task 004); Route uses the task 012 registry (no harness or confidence below 0.85 → hand-off to the triage stage slot, task 016); Analyse/Build/Persist delegate to the harness; Approve sets AwaitingApproval and stops (the approval Work Item is task 017); Return/Record slots exist with markers (door-specific return bodies are later tasks); crash-injection and duplicate-delivery tests prove FR-07(a–e).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07 (acceptance a–e), NFR-01, NFR-06, NFR-08, design §3.3 (step-0 rules) and §4 (ADR-052 written reason); MUST rules: atomic receive-side idempotency (`IIdempotencyService` alone is check-then-set and fails open, #984; project CLAUDE.md §6), terminal status last, no content in payloads/logs. The run record is `sprk_processingjob` extended by task 011 (request lookup, harness key, engine execution id, staging prefix, re-drive marker; stages in `sprk_currentstage`/`sprk_stages`); the request is `sprk_servicerequest` (task 010: stage, current run, correlation id). Stage writes to the request are owned here (ADR-002 single writer). Triage threshold 0.85 (spec Assumptions). Engine dispatch/completion is task 014; NDA harness 015; triage body 016.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRunJobHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRunStore.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/IntakePipelineOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/IntakeRunJobHandlerTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/IntakeRunResumeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/JobProcessingModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs:71 (READ ONLY — frozen until eBilling UAT)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Jobs/InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs:66 (resume from stored state; READ ONLY)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandlerTests.cs (test structure to copy)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/JobContract.cs (MaxDeliveryCount :65), src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs (lock API; not sufficient alone)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/IntakeHarnessRegistry.cs (task 012), src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IAgreementAi.cs (task 004)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="004" status="pending">IAgreementAi.ClassifyAsync for the Classify stage.</dependency>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Request columns (stage, current run, correlation id).</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Run columns (request lookup, harness key, markers, Intake run job type).</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">RequestType routing key and harness registry.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: IntakeRunJobHandler. Implements `IJobHandler` dispatched by `ServiceBusJobProcessor`; receive-side claim is atomic (conditional create/upsert or Dataverse If-Match on the run row, A1 §4) — never `IIdempotencyService` check-then-set alone; payload is ids only (request id, run id, correlationId).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-017">Scope: every stage transition. Persisted on the run (and the request stage) with idempotent writes; the terminal status (Completed / Failed / held-for-attention) is written last, after every side effect of the run.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: AI stages (Classify, Analyse). A stage whose result is persisted is never re-executed on resume or redelivery; "Processing" is written before any AI call; deterministic ids/keys for every created record and message; a marker is written before any send (FR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Scope: kill switches. `IntakePipelineOptions` exposes per-door and per-harness enable flags read at run time (config change, no redeploy); a disabled harness holds the run with admin-attention text (not Failed, not Completed); a disabled door is enforced by the door tasks using the same options.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: logs, telemetry, exceptions and `sprk_payload`/`sprk_result`. Ids, stage names, outcome and error codes only; no document text, classification reasoning text or plan content.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: request stage, current run and run status. Written only by this orchestrator (and later the approval endpoint), never by clients.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this task. Do NOT edit `InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs`, `InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs` or anything under `Services/Finance/Submission/`; no hand-rolled `BackgroundService`; no Durable Task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Scope: the PR. State the Placement Justification (ADR-052 written reason, design §4), measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build, ≤ 60 MB total, no new package and no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

