  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the invoice handler and rerun handler (read only) and design §3.3; write the stage table (stage → persisted result → idempotency key → resume rule) into the task notes before coding.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement IntakeRunStore: read run + request; conditional (If-Match) stage/status writes; atomic claim per message.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement IntakeRunJobHandler: step-0 rules; stages 1–10 with stored-state resume; Classify via IAgreementAi; Route via the registry (no harness or confidence below 0.85 → triage slot); harness delegation for Analyse/Build/Persist; Approve = AwaitingApproval wait; Return/Record slots with markers; terminal last; final-delivery → admin-attention text and DLQ (never "Completed").</step>
    <step order="4">Add IntakePipelineOptions (per-door, per-harness flags) and register the handler and options in JobProcessingModule.</step>
    <step order="5">Write tests: crash injected after each stage resumes at that stage with zero repeat AI calls; duplicate delivery → no duplicate creates/messages; terminal run redelivered → no-op; exhausted run → DLQ outcome with admin text; disabled harness → held; payload/log capture contains no content.</step>
    <step order="6">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`; measure publish size vs fresh master.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If an atomic claim cannot be implemented with existing primitives (Dataverse If-Match, BlobGateway.CreateIfNotExistsAsync, Redis SET NX) without a new package or service, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>If resume-without-re-running-AI requires persisting AI output content on the run row (ADR-015), STOP and escalate with options (outputs stored as sprk_analysis/sprk_document and referenced by id).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the frozen invoice handler would need a change to share code, STOP — copy the rule instead; never edit it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 1 (multi-stage resumable orchestrator): `InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs:71`, `InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs:66`, `ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs` (CAPABILITY-INDEX row 6); verdict "new handler on the existing framework; copy the invoice rules".</existing>
    <extension>No — the invoice handlers are invoice-typed throughout and frozen until eBilling UAT (design §7, Q4); the generic framework (IJobHandler, JobContract) is reused as is.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Front Door, Console and email requests are never processed: no stage advances, nothing reaches AwaitingApproval (FR-07, success criterion 4).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

