  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a crash injected after each stage, redelivery resumes at that stage and the AI facade/harness is not called again for any stage whose result was persisted (FR-07a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same message delivered twice (including concurrently), exactly one set of documents, analyses, Work Items, messages and emails is created (FR-07b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a run already in a terminal state, redelivery is a no-op (FR-07c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an exhausted run (final delivery failed) is dead-lettered with admin-attention text and its status is never "Completed" (FR-07d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: captured queue payloads and logs contain no document content (FR-07e); every log scope carries the run's correlationId (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given no harness for the request type, or classification confidence below 0.85, the run hands off to the triage slot and is not Failed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a harness disabled in IntakePipelineOptions, the run is held with admin-attention text; re-enabling and re-driving resumes it (NFR-08).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The terminal status write is the last write of a run (asserted by write-order in tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs`, `InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs` and `Services/Finance/Submission/**` are unchanged; DiGraphValidationTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PR states Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Seeding proofs requested for (1) the atomic claim — replace it with check-then-set, confirm the concurrent-duplicate test fails, restore; (2) resume — drop the persisted-result check for Analyse, confirm the no-repeat-AI test fails, restore. Brief deviation: deps add 004 (Classify stage uses IAgreementAi). Door-specific Return bodies (Front Door 021, email 043) and the approval Work Item (017) plug into the slots defined here. Task 011 column facts (notes/011-processingjob-run-columns.md): job type &quot;Intake run&quot; = 7 (ProcessingJobType.IntakeRun); lookups sprk_servicerequest / sprk_outputdocument bind as sprk_ServiceRequest@odata.bind / sprk_OutputDocument@odata.bind; sprk_redrivecount has no default, treat null as 0. Write-path gap found by 011: CreateProcessingJobAsync and UpdateProcessingJobAsync write a bare Guid to lookup columns (only sprk_initiatedby is special-cased), which Dataverse rejects, so this task must add EntityReference handling for the two new lookups or the first run create fails. The Office read path already returns not-found for job type 7 (OfficeJobStatusService.IsIntakeRun). Open design point from task 012 (notes/012-routing-key-harness-registry.md): IIntakeHarness.RunAsync is one call, so the orchestrator cannot persist the edit plan between Analyse and Build as task 015 expects; decide here whether to split RunAsync into Analyse and Build (resume must never re-run the AI step, FR-07).</notes>

